# Laboratory Maniac: "If you would draw a card while your library has no cards in it, you win the game instead" (CR 614.1a,
# 121.6). Bot1's deck is eight cards, so after its opening hand its library holds one. Ancestral Recall has Bot1 draw three, each
# draw on its own (CR 121.2): the first finds the library with a card in it and draws it as usual; the second would be from an
# empty library and is replaced - Bot1 wins the game (CR 104.2b) there and then, rather than losing for drawing from an empty
# library (CR 704.5b).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Laboratory Maniac
Ancestral Recall
Island
Island
Island

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Laboratory Maniac.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Result = Bot1 won
Bot2.Status = Lost
Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
Bot1.Library.Count = 0
